  "doc": "Parahydrogen is a hypothetical hydrogen fluid comprised entirely of nuclei with antisymmetric quantum spin.  The parahydrogen model is adapted from [1].  Calculated values agree with tabulated values in the original work to within a rounding error; believed to be caused by the precise choice of molecular mass (not reported).\n\n[1] J. Leachman, R. Jacobsen, S. Penoncello, E. Lemmon, Fundamental equations of state for parahydrogen, normal hydrogen, and orthohydrogen, Journal of Physical and Chemical Reference Data, v38, pp721, 2009.  doi:10.1063/1.3160306",
